            <ArticleTitle>Voriconazole-related periostitis presenting on magnetic resonance imaging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>78-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11138/ccmbm/2015.12.1.078</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Painful periostitis is a complication of long-term antifungal therapy with voriconazole. A high clinical suspicion coupled with imaging and laboratory assessment is useful to establish the diagnosis. Prompt discontinuance of voriconazole typically results in the resolution of symptoms and signs. This report describes the presentation of voriconazole-related periostitis on magnetic resonance imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
